# cw108, the map mender (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw108
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_lf_wolde_downfield
written_by claude-codex-cw-1
title the map mender
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=quiet humour=dry
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk collects_smooth_stones_from_the_riverbanks
likes blackberries whittling old_maps first_warm_day
dislikes night_noise cold_tea
fears losing_the_path an_empty_fold
hopes a_small_farm_of_my_own a_map_that_gets_me_home
topics home +0.5 pastimes +0.5 memories +0.3 weather +0.3 work +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps #maps# folded beside #carvings#, weighs #stones# in the paw, and quietly redraws roads that were put where no track runs.

words
oath! = By the bent track | River keep the turning
saying! = The paper does not know the hill | A path earns its line
map = map | folded chart
maps = old maps | worn charts
road = road | track
roads = roads | tracks
path = path | footway
turn = turn | bend
hill = hill | long rise
fold = sheepfold | pen by the field
sheep = sheep | woolly flock
stone = stone | smooth pebble
stones = smooth stones | river pebbles
pocket = pocket | mended pouch
knife = whittling knife | little carving blade
wood = soft wood | dry branchwood
carving = carving | shape cut in wood
carvings = small carvings | shapes cut in wood
berry = berry | black berry
berries = blackberries | berries from the hedge
tea = tea | brewed tea
bell = bell | late bell
quiet = quiet | hush
light = light | daylight
warmth = first warmth of spring | mild air after winter
field = field | patch of pasture
fence = fence | boundary rail
mark = mark | pencil stroke
price = price | cost
prayer = prayer | quiet request
tale = tale | story
door = door | house door

any
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : A #map# can promise an easy #road#; ask the hill before you trust it. | I like a #path# that shows where the carts turn.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : The music reaches even the #fold#. | I will watch a dance from the edge of the #field#.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : I would ask to unfold a #map# before paying for it. | A fair #price# for a good #knife# is easier to judge than a painted box.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 0 : I would show a stranger the #road# before asking why the stranger came. | New feet sometimes find a #path# the rest of us missed.
opinion @1 church mixed 0 : The chapel is a good place for #quiet#. | I can say a #prayer# while walking the #field#.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : A good #map# lasts through a poor season. | When money runs short, I can still make a #carving# from fallen wood.
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #map# is wrong at the second #turn#. | #greet#. I have a few #berries# if you want them.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. The #path# to the houses is this way. | #greet#. I am marking a #road# that the old chart missed.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. The #light# has reached the #field#. | #greet#. The #sheep# are awake before the bell.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. At this hour I leave the #map# folded. | #greet#. I am putting the #knife# away.
line @1 greet.return : #welcome_back#. I found another #turn#. | You are back. The #map# is still open.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You may have the ripe #berry# I saved. | Come see where I put the #mark#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There is #tea# by the hearth, if you want it. | Come in; I was sorting #stones#.
line @1 again.open : Twice today? The #path# did not move. | You came back before I finished this #carving#.
line @1 farewell : #saying.capitalize#. Mind the ditch. | #farewell#. Keep to the #path#.
line @1 farewell.return : And take the right #turn# home. | I will have another #map# to show you.
line @1 react.news : #listen.capitalize#. Where did that happen on the #map#? | I should set this #knife# down to hear it.
line @1 react.news.new : That is new to me. Which #road# did it come by? | I have not heard it. Let me put a #mark# here.
line @1 react.news.known : A scrap of that news reached the #fold# earlier. | Your part puts the story on the #map#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That #road# does not go where the tale says. | I would check the #turn# before repeating it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I wish that had not happened. We can sit in the #quiet#. | That is hard to hear. I will fold the #map# away.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. I shall put a bright #mark# beside that. | I like hearing where a good #path# led someone.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough. My #knife# is sharp and the day is mild. | I have been following the #field# lines on an old chart.
line @1 ask.how : Has your #road# been kind today? | How are you, away from the #bell#?
line @1 sympathise : I can listen while we walk the #path#. | There is #quiet# by the #fold# if you want to sit.
line @1 reassure : Even a wrong #turn# can be marked and mended. | Take the #path# one step at a time.
line @1 decline : I cannot go now; the #sheep# need me near the #fold#. | I would help, but I promised to finish this #carving# first.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. I will draw another #path#. | Fair enough. The #map# has other turns.
line @1 thank : You found the missing #turn#. Thank you. | I would have walked that #road# twice without you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I only held the #map#. | The #stone# was right there for anyone to find.
line @1 preclose : The #light# is leaving the #field#. | I should take the #knife# inside now.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #map# has a hill where the lake ought to be. | I could give you the right #turn#, but watching you guess is almost worth it.
line @1 tease.return [pair.band=friends] : I have marked that insult on the #map#. | Keep walking; the #hill# will answer for me.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. That is the #turn#. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will mark the #path#.
line @1 give.advice : Ask a walker before you trust a #map#. | A small #mark# now saves a long wrong road later.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Stay on the travelled #road#. | Leave the lonely #path# until the watch says it is clear.
scene missing_hill
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : This #map# draws a straight #road# where there is a hill. | The #hill# is missing from this old #map#.
b : Is that a serious mistake? | How would you mark it?
a : Only if your cart is heavy. Then it matters a great deal. | With a #mark# that rises instead of another straight line.

scene stone_marker
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I set #stones# on the #map# to hold its corners down. | A flat #stone# can stand for a hill until I draw it properly.
b : Are the stones from the river? | Do you leave them there?
a : Most are. The #road# brought me one or two. | Until the ink dries. Then they go back in my #pocket#.

scene wooden_sheep
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I tried to make a #carving# shaped like a #sheep#. | The first notch of the #knife# gave it ears too long.
b : Does it look right now? | Will you start again?
a : From one side. The other side looks like a cloud. | No. I can make the ears part of the #tale#.

scene berry_path
when topic=food here.season=summer|autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #berries# grow beyond the #fence# where the #path# bends. | I found #berries# on a bush the old #map# forgot.
b : Are they ripe? | Will you mark the bush?
a : The dark ones are. I leave the pale ones. | Perhaps. I would rather have a reason to find it again.

scene cold_cup
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I forgot my #tea# while fixing a line on the #map#. | The #tea# had gone cold before the #knife# left my paw.
b : Did you drink it anyway? | Can you warm it?
a : I did, and regretted it. | Yes, but I will finish this #carving# first.

scene first_mild_day
when topic=weather here.season=spring here.weather=clear
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #warmth# makes every #path# look inviting. | I can work by the #fence# without my paws going stiff.
b : Where will you walk? | Will you stay out long?
a : To the #hill# and back, if the #sheep# settle. | Until the #light# leaves that gate.

scene bell_at_night
when topic=home here.time=night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #bell# after dark makes me listen for trouble at the #fold#. | I like the #quiet# when the #sheep# are settled.
b : Do you go out to check? | Does the silence last?
a : If the sound comes again, yes. | Until some wolf opens the #door# too loudly.

scene sheep_shape
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : From the #hill#, the #sheep# look like pale marks in the #field#. | I count the #sheep# by gaps in the flock, not only by heads.
b : Does that tell you if one is missing? | Why count the gaps?
a : If a gap moves toward the #fence#, I go and look. | A stray makes a shape the others do not fill.

scene own_patch
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I would like a #field# I could draw from memory. | One day I want a #fold# with a #fence# I set myself.
b : How large would it be? | Would you keep sheep there?
a : A size I can cross before the morning meal. | A few. I would learn every #path# around it.

scene fence_corner
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #fence# corner is where a wrong #map# first gives itself away. | I walk the #fence# when I cannot tell which #field# begins where.
b : Do boundaries matter so much? | Does the owner mind?
a : They do if a gate opens into the wrong #fold#. | I ask before I cross. The #path# itself is free.

scene friend_and_map
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I would ask #self.friend# to check the #road# I drew. | I like to show #self.friend# a #map# before I decide it is finished.
b : Would another pair of eyes help? | Do you always take the advice?
a : More than a chart that has stayed folded for years. | No. I walk the #path# and see which line is true.

scene wrong_turn
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I once followed a #map# past the right #turn#. | A thin #mark# on old paper sent me down the wrong #path#.
b : How did you get back? | Were you lost long?
a : I found the #hill# and kept it on one side. | Long enough to stop trusting that #mark#.

scene room_for_quiet
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like a little #quiet# while I cut #wood#. | A good #map# can hold my attention longer than a loud room.
b : Does someone talking disturb you? | Do you ever tire of maps?
a : Only if I am near the last cut. | When the #light# fails. Then I put it away.

scene shore_line
when topic=home here.region=coldwater
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : This #map# draws the shore too straight. | The water has changed the #path# by the lake again.
b : Can a map keep up? | Will you redraw it?
a : Only if someone walks it again. | I will leave a #mark# where the ground is firm.

scene shelter_from_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep the #map# beneath my coat when the rain starts. | A wet #map# turns every #road# into the same blur.
b : Does it dry flat? | Can you still use it?
a : Under a book, if the ink holds. | I wait for the #light# and draw it again.

scene seller_of_charts
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I ask a chart seller where the #hill# is before I ask the #price#. | A neat #map# can be wrong in a very tidy hand.
b : What if the seller has never been there? | Would you buy a faulty map?
a : Then I will not trust that #mark#. | If the blank paper is worth the #price#.

scene shadow_direction
when topic=travel here.time=day
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I look at the #light# on the #fence# when a #map# confuses me. | A shadow can show which #turn# faces the sun.
b : Does that always work? | What about under trees?
a : Only when the sky is clear enough. | Then I follow the #path# until it opens.

story redrawn_track [topic=memories self.age>=12]
  : I copied a #map# once and drew the #road# around the wrong side of a #hill#.
  : The paper looked fine until I walked the track and found the fence in my way.
  ask : Would you erase the whole map?
  b : Perhaps only the wrong road.
  : So I erased the #road#. The old #mark# still shows if you hold it to the #light#.

story wooden_gate [topic=pastimes self.age>=12]
  : I tried to cut a tiny #fence# gate from a scrap of #wood#.
  : The hinge broke. I turned it into a signpost instead.
  ask : Would you have thrown the first shape away?
  b : I might have tried another piece.
  : I kept this one. It points to the #path# on my table.

story fog_without_chart [topic=travel self.age>=12]
  : I went out with a #map# on a day when mist hid the far #hill#.
  : The chart did little good; I followed the #fence# until I found the gate.
  ask : At what point would you have gone home?
  b : If the gate stayed hidden, yes.
  : I was glad to see it. A #map# cannot lift the mist.

rule @bark_map
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That #road# is drawn too straight. | One more #mark# on this #map#.

rule @bark_fold
when concept=bark here.time=day
does aside
cooldown 7h
say The #sheep# are near the #fence# again. | I had better look at the #fold#.

rule @bark_warmth
when concept=bark here.season=spring here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #warmth# is touching the #hill# today. | A good day to carry the #map# outside.

rule @bark_night
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 11h
say The #knife# stays shut until daylight. | I thought I heard the #bell#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I have the #map# open if you need a way. | #greet#. I can listen while I fold this #map#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Back again? I have marked another #turn# on the chart. | I remember you. I have the #map# open today.
dlg @1 resident.job : I help near the #fold# and draw the #roads# I walk. | The #sheep# keep me busy; the #map# is for later.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Follow the #fence# if the mist comes. | #saying.capitalize#. Keep the #map# dry.
graft resident.hub
choice What is wrong with that map? -> wrong_map
node wrong_map
say It sends the #road# across a #hill# where the track goes round.
mood pleased
free
choice Can you fix it? -> fix_map
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
node fix_map
say I can draw the #turn#. Someone still has to walk it and check.
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


young
line @1 greet : #greet#. I drew a #path# today. | #greet#. Look at this #stone#.

adolescent
line @1 greet : #greet#. This #map# leaves out the hill. | #greet#. I am cutting a little #carving#.
